(Brajesh K Singh) writes:
>> There's a bug in Nethack that lets monsters throw items at you even
>> while you're invisible.
>
>   Being invisible doesn't make you stealthy.

Does it make you pedantic?

Frankly, for all intents and purposes, invisibility does make you
stealthy.  Monsters don't track you while you're invisible, for
instance.  Regardless, the point is that monsters only care if you're
on line with them when they throw things, and that's wrong.  If you 
want to implement some clever code that does something to make monsters
track you by ear, go right ahead.  Meanwhile, the code that is there
is obviously wrong.

